[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/985","id":4267217573,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSeuyxc7-WJKl","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/985","diff_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/985.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/985.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/issues/985","number":985,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(pipeline): phase 6 — per-stage models and the local-model advisor","user":{"login":"saeedkolivand","id":51081940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDgxOTQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51081940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Phase 6 of the staged résumé pipeline: **per-stage AI models + the local-model advisor**. Follows #971 (eval harness).\n\n## What it does\n\n- **Per-stage model overrides**: each paying pipeline stage (analyze → evidence → strategy → draft/sections → repair → judge) can run on its own provider+model, stored in a new `ai_stage_overrides` table on the AI config store (append-only migration), resolved through `Completer::from_active_for_stage` with the exact same validate/SSRF chain as the active config. Free stages (assemble/validate) are rejected at write, import, and read — the reject set is codegen'd from the pipeline truth (`PIPELINE_STAGES_FREE`) so it cannot drift. **No per-stage `base_url` exists, structurally**: security review showed an accepted-but-undisplayed egress field is a covert channel even when validated, so the column was removed and resolve-time follows the one URL Settings displays.\n- **Per-stage cache keys**: `StageCacheKey` now carries provider+model+context_window per stage (`StageIdentity`) — two configs differing in one stage's override cache separately for that stage and share everything else. The window joined the key because it changes what the model sees (`num_ctx`), the review's \"clean regression\" catch.\n- **Context-window threading**: the user's configured window now reaches staged Ollama calls (it previously reached only the fast path — every staged run silently used the 2048 default). Bounds enforced at write, patch, import, resolve, and both wire entrypoints. A one-shot backfill promotes existing installs' configured windows so the fix reaches upgrading users, not just new ones.\n- **PATCH provider settings**: `set_provider_settings` is now non-destructive on absence server-side (absent = keep, explicit null = clear, value = set) — the old REPLACE contract had already silently erased fields at three call sites.\n- **Settings UI**: a per-stage overrides card (effective model per stage, plain-language stage descriptions, card-level vs per-row warnings), a suggested-smaller-model banner for the extraction stages (measured `parameterSize` on both sides required — never the tier fallback; one-click accept, never silent), and a 4-step **Model advisor** wizard: installed models → context-fit against the real stage prompt budgets → recommendations (app-does-this vs advice-you-run-yourself, strictly separated) → thinking-model risk (spend-store data where providers report it, honest \"not measured ≠ safe\" copy elsewhere).\n- **Spend store**: `thinking_tokens` column recorded where providers genuinely report the split (OpenAI `reasoning_tokens`, Gemini `thoughtsTokenCount`); NULL elsewhere — absence of data is never presented as absence of risk.\n- **Restore resilience**: one malformed row (or entry) in a backup's provider/override maps is dropped per-row instead of failing the whole section restore — tolerance at both the type and entry level, probed with `-1`, `2^32`, wrong-typed and string entries.\n\n## Review provenance\n\nSeven internal rounds before this PR: ai-provider-expert (BLOCK → fix → delta APPROVE → advisories), frontend-reviewer + ui-ux-expert on the renderer (both BLOCK: the suggestion heuristic recommending a 70B/embedding model as \"smaller\", measured AA contrast failures, a modal focus escape — all fixed with executed evidence), tauri-security-reviewer (APPROVE + the covert-channel finding that removed the per-stage base_url), and a 3-pass ensemble (BLOCK → 4 HIGHs fixed, incl. a 3-pass-consensus ref-scoping bug in the window-commit latch and the missing upgrade backfill). ~100 findings closed across the rounds, all red-first with executed mutations; reviewer prescriptions disproven and corrected in both directions along the way.\n\n## Tests\n\n4049 Rust lib + 18 architecture; renderer vitest 3471+ (incl. new StageOverrideEditor / LocalModelLimits / ModelAdvisor suites); i18n en+de key resolution executed against the real i18next instance; clippy `--all-targets --all-features --locked -D warnings`, fmt, gen:ipc drift gate, lint:strict + a11y lint — all green. Zero new dependencies; lockfiles unchanged.\n\nRider: a one-line structural read fixes the pre-existing `router-guard.ts` TanStack type drift that blocked the frontend typecheck gate (present on main).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-08-13T01:07:42Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T01:29:10Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"423cca68c60ab2c74c4bca79d3970995f64b576e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10964600421,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACjYqGZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"description":"Documentation and markdown"},{"id":11212541200,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNEA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/app/desktop","name":"app/desktop","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Changes to apps/desktop"},{"id":11212541282,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/pkg/shared","name":"pkg/shared","color":"1abc9c","default":false,"description":"Changes to packages/shared"},{"id":11212541489,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHOMQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/pkg/translations","name":"pkg/translations","color":"20c997","default":false,"description":"Changes to packages/translations"},{"id":11212541572,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHOhA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/rust","name":"rust","color":"dea584","default":false,"description":"Rust backend (apps/desktop/src-tauri)"},{"id":11212541661,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHO3Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/frontend","name":"frontend","color":"7057ff","default":false,"description":"React renderer (apps/desktop/src/renderer)"}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/985/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/985/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"